# assistente utile U1+U2 (docs/plans/assistente-utile.md) — la situazione di chi
# parla esegue il piano di condotta insegnato parlando. I piani veri sono quelli
# salvati dalla sessione di addestramento (kb/core/messages.p0); qui si provano
# la meccanica, l'ablation e il ripristino, e il file lascia il piano com'era.
[mock live]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test the speaker's problem runs the taught plan]
!timeout 30
> I have a problem with my bike.
<~ Let's look at it together.
<~ What is it, and what exactly happens?
> My phone screen is broken.
<~ Let's look at it together.
> the heating is broken
<~ Let's look at it together.

[test a settled problem and a topic named problem do not run it]
!timeout 30
> I solved the problem with my bike.
<! Let's look at it together
> the problem with this theory is its size
<! Let's look at it together

[test a worry is not answered as good news]
!timeout 30
> I'm really stressed about my exam tomorrow.
<~ That sounds hard
<! sounds nice
> I'm really happy about my exam result.
<! That sounds hard

[test sadness has its own plan, and an italian worry gets the taught plan]
!timeout 30
> I feel sad today
<~ I'm sorry you're feeling this way.
<! sounds nice
> the song is sad
<! I'm sorry
> Sono preoccupato per il colloquio di lavoro di domani.
<! being worried is a reason

[test a choice between two things gets criteria and the deciding question]
!timeout 30
> Should I learn Python or JavaScript first?
<~ it depends on what you need it for
<! what you mean by
> should i go?
<! it depends on what you need

[test asking what help is available is answered for the user, not from the ledger]
!timeout 30
> What can you help me with?
<~ I can help you think through a problem
<~ What do you need right now?
<! capability ledger

[test help writing a message gets the shape and the question, code stays code]
!timeout 30
> Help me write an email.
<~ A clear message puts the main point
<~ Who is it for
<! no code to show
> write a python function that sorts a list
<! A clear message

[test starting something new gets the first step and the time question]
!timeout 30
> I want to learn to cook. Where should I start?
<~ Start small and regular
<~ How much time can you give it each week?
> where does the river begin?
<! Start small

[test organizing the day gets the method and the question, in italian too]
!timeout 30
> Come posso organizzare meglio la mia giornata?
<~ Scrivi che cosa devi fare
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
> How can I organize my day better?
<~ Write down what you have to do

[test gift ideas get directions and the narrowing question, a class present does not]
!timeout 30
> Give me some ideas for a birthday present for my dad.
<~ A few directions that often work
<~ What does the person enjoy
> the present for the class is a test
<! A few directions

[test a plan lesson that names the situation is a lesson, not the situation]
!timeout 30
> when someone needs gift ideas then ask what the person enjoys
<~ Already in the plan
<! A few directions

[test the plan is taught knowledge: unlearn it and the situation says nothing]
!timeout 30
> unlearn what you do when someone has a problem
<~ Forgotten
> I have a problem with my bike.
<! Let's look at it together

[test a when-then lesson is a statement, a when-question is still a question]
!timeout 30
> when someone has a problem then say we will look at it together
<~ Held: in that situation, move 1
> when did someone have a problem?
<! Held
> when someone has a problem then remind them about safety
<~ move 2
> when someone has a problem then ask what it is and what happens
<~ move 3
<! refer to
> I have a problem with my bike.
<~ Let's look at it together. If something smokes
